# "Vector Operands" (vreg_overlap_legal, vreg_source_eew_rsv) is derived from the element widths: a destination keeps
# from each source of another width with constraint.BY_WIDTHS, and two sources of different widths keep apart with
# constraint.SAME_WIDTH. a source is a vector argument the row reads as an operand, the destination where
# effects.RECASTS states it read, never for the undisturbed policies' read. a pair a KEEPS row keeps apart whole states
# no rule of its widths, and a reduction's destination keeps from nothing: "Vector Reduction Operations"
# (vreduction_vd_overlap_vs), its destination may overlap the source operands, including the mask register
#
# "Vector Masking" (vreg_vmask_rsv): a masked instruction's destination cannot overlap the mask register v0, unless
# it is written with a mask value, as by a compare, or with a reduction's scalar. every vector row with a vm argument
# keeps a vd that is neither a mask nor a scalar from MASK_REGISTER while vm is v0.t. and as vreg_source_eew_rsv
# reads a mask source at width 1, each source of another width keeps from MASK_REGISTER while vm is v0.t, and always
# in the rows of MASK_READERS, which read v0 as a mask whatever their encoding
pub val MASK_ARG:      str = "vm";
pub val MASK_REGISTER: str = "v0";

pub val MASK_READERS_COUNT: u32 = 6;

pub val MASK_READERS: [MASK_READERS_COUNT]str = [MASK_READERS_COUNT]str{"vadc.v*m", "vsbc.v*m", "vmerge.v*m", "vmadc.v*m", "vmsbc.v*m", "vfmerge.vfm"};

# "Vector Load/Store Instruction Encoding" and "Vector Load/Store Width Encoding": a vector load or store, in the
# LOAD-FP or STORE-FP major opcode with a width of 0, 5, 6 or 7, encodes EEW in width (bits 14 to 12), the
# addressing mode in mop (bits 27 to 26) and a unit-stride variant in lumop or sumop (bits 24 to 20). unit-stride and
# constant-stride rows hold their data at that EEW, and indexed rows (mop 1 and 3) their index vs2, their data at SEW.
# a whole register row (lumop 8) covers nf + 1 registers ("Vector Load/Store Whole Register Instructions"), and a
# mask row (lumop 11) one register at EEW=8 ("Vector Unit-Stride Instructions")
pub val WIDTH_LO:    u64 = 12;
pub val MOP_LO:      u64 = 26;
pub val LUMOP_LO:    u64 = 20;
pub val WHOLE_LUMOP: u64 = 8;
pub val MASK_LUMOP:  u64 = 11;
pub val INDEXED_MOP: u64 = 1;

# "Vector Load/Store Segment Instructions": the data operand of a segment load or store covers one group per field,
# nf + 1 of them, nf being bits 31 to 29 of the encoding
# ---
# mnemonic: the rows it applies to
# arg:      their data operand
pub rec Segment {
    mnemonic: str;
    arg:      str;
}

pub val SEGMENTS_COUNT: u32 = 8;

pub val SEGMENTS: [SEGMENTS_COUNT]Segment = [SEGMENTS_COUNT]Segment{
    Segment{mnemonic: "vlseg*", arg: "vd"},
    Segment{mnemonic: "vlsseg*", arg: "vd"},
    Segment{mnemonic: "vluxseg*", arg: "vd"},
    Segment{mnemonic: "vloxseg*", arg: "vd"},
    Segment{mnemonic: "vsseg*", arg: "vs3"},
    Segment{mnemonic: "vssseg*", arg: "vs3"},
    Segment{mnemonic: "vsuxseg*", arg: "vs3"},
    Segment{mnemonic: "vsoxseg*", arg: "vs3"},
};

pub val NF_LO: u64 = 29;
